WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
GENESIS: JURIS Studio. Five Flats, Three Countries. End to end, inside Studio.

00:07.000 --> 00:20.000
Studio opens in User View. Technical identifiers stay out of the way while the professional workflow remains available. This walkthrough follows one canonical case from instruction to client-ready report.

00:20.000 --> 00:38.000
Start with one compact instruction: a PRC resident plans to buy five English flats for £1 million, using 80% financing at 7.5%, with Liechtenstein in the route and a 10% annual-return target.

00:38.000 --> 01:00.000
Understand with AI does not silently rewrite the case. It expands the one-line brief into a read-only canonical proposal: mandate, jurisdictions, fixed facts, open assumptions, return definitions, lawful baseline, risks, evidence gates and stop conditions. The author reviews it before accepting anything.

01:00.000 --> 01:24.000
Next, close the financial gaps. Set interest-only debt, 5% vacancy, 10% management, 5% repairs, documented insurance and compliance costs, £15,000 setup and £10,000 annual administration. The downside remains explicit: lower rent, extended vacancy and a year-two repair.

01:24.000 --> 01:44.000
Now Studio generates the graph from the reviewed prompt and parameters. The result contains 27 semantic nodes and 31 explicit connections covering the client, property, financing, operating model, evidence, three-country tax gates, baseline comparison, decisions and adverse outcomes.

01:44.000 --> 02:02.000
Select a node to inspect its source, conditions and consequences. The return node keeps four meanings separate: gross yield, NOI yield, pre-tax cash-on-cash and ten-year after-tax equity IRR. Links stay editable, and every change can be undone.

02:02.000 --> 02:24.000
Outcome calculation stays transparent. From the reviewed income and costs, Studio calculates £24,328 annual cash flow. On £215,000 of initial equity, pre-tax cash-on-cash is 11.3%, and debt-service coverage is 1.41x.

02:24.000 --> 02:48.000
Finally, generate the PDF inside Studio. The report uses the same reviewed graph and includes the case overview, economics, scenario analysis, decision map, facts and evidence register, authorities, node conditions, verification checklist and fingerprint. The raw AI prompt is excluded.

02:48.000 --> 03:00.000
One case, one Studio, fully auditable. AI proposes, the professional verifies, and Studio preserves the exact prompt, graph, outcome and report.
